---
description: Phrase routing and router corpus
globs: kuro-rs/crates/kuro-router/**,kuro-rs/fixtures/phrases/**
alwaysApply: false
---
Add the failing corpus case in `fixtures/phrases/` before fixing routing.
The router classifies and ranks only; it never executes tools or side effects.
Phrase data lives in fixtures and TOML, not hard-coded in unrelated crates.
Changing a threshold or stage order needs a corpus diff in the PR description.
Keep normalization and semantic stages testable without network or ONNX at gate time.
Refactor PRs must leave golden corpus files byte-identical.
Run router crate tests and `cargo xtask gate fast` before finishing.
Do not pull shell or WinUI dependencies into `kuro-router`.